{% doc %}
  Renders the bundled lifestyle photo that belongs to a collection, so every collection has a face before the merchant
  uploads an image. Each scene shows a pen from that collection (the burl scene the burl pen, `skyline` the marbled
  resin pen, and so on); `gifts` takes the pen on the display stand, since it has no pen of its own. Renders nothing for
  any other handle, so those fall back to their first pen's photo.

  The handles are placeholders, like the ones in templates/index.json: they must match the store's collections.

  @param {string} handle - The collection handle: `burl-wood`, `hardwood`, `laminated-wood`, `resin` or `gifts`.
  @param {string} [class] - Extra CSS classes for the image.
  @param {string} [loading] - `lazy` (default) or `eager`.

  @example
  {% render 'pegasus-collection-photo', handle: collection.handle, class: 'motion-reduce' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign scene = null
  case handle
    when 'burl-wood'
      assign scene = 'burl'
    when 'hardwood'
      assign scene = 'stone'
    when 'laminated-wood'
      assign scene = 'leather'
    when 'resin'
      assign scene = 'skyline'
    when 'gifts'
      assign scene = 'desk'
  endcase
-%}
{%- if scene -%}
  {% render 'pegasus-scene', name: scene, class: class, loading: loading %}
{%- endif -%}
